  "market_context": "Daily chart showing a clear downtrend with lower highs and lower lows. A key resistance zone formed where prior support turned resistance converged with a descending trendline connecting swing highs. Price approached this confluence area during a short-term uptrend phase.",
  "key_observation": "Price reacted at the confluence of a descending trendline and a former support-turned-resistance level (around 1.03500–1.04000) with a bearish engulfing candle, rejecting upward movement without breaking the zone.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the primary market structure as a daily downtrend (lower highs and lower lows).",
    "Step 2: Draw a descending trendline connecting three swing highs to define dynamic resistance.",
    "Step 3: Locate a prior support level that had turned into resistance (around 1.03500–1.04000) on the left side of the chart.",
    "Step 4: Recognize the confluence zone where the trendline and the S/R level intersect, labeling it as an area of high convergence.",
    "Step 5: Observe price action at the confluence: a bearish engulfing candle rejected the zone without breaking through.",
    "Step 6: Note the secondary short-term uptrend and wait for its trendline break to confirm bearish continuation before entering."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "A confluence of trendline and S/R increases probability of reaction, but trade entry requires confirmation—here, the engulfing rejection plus subsequent break of the short-term uptrend line validated the primary downtrend continuation.",
